    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1354">

                <pb facs="0906" n="790" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg790"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/156c.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Special Agent
                        Carothers.</hi><anchor n="112" xml:id="d1354-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 6, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Have been shown Associated Press dispatch stating that Villa is anxious to have
                    the Spanish Ambassador at Washington know that <pb facs="0907" n="791"
                        xml:id="pg791"/> Spaniards in Torreon may expect no mercy. He is reported as
                    requesting that the Ambassador be advised that Spaniards had better get out
                    while they can. Please see Villa at once and say that the United States cannot
                    believe that the report is authentic but we feel compelled to protest in the
                    most emphatic terms against cruelty to foreigners whether Spaniards or citizens
                    of other countries. We are sure that Villa will on reflection realize the
                    importance of observing the rules of war and respect the person and property of
                    foreigners.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1354-f1" n="112" type="source" xml:id="d1354-f1-content">
                <p>Same telegram to the Consuls at Chihuahua and Hermosillo. See also footnote
                    114.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
